    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We extend minimum curvature splines used for geologic surface interpolations by treating the interpolated surface as an elastic plate with finite thickness. The finite thickness plate may reflect the process by which lithologic layers are deformed more accurately and permit the prescription of both known elevation and slopes of the layers simultaneously.We solve the resulting problem using the finite element method. The results of these finite thickness plate interpolations improve interpolations for given surface geometries when compared.to minimum curvature splines and thus offer a viable alternative to commonly employed methods.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
